  "step_3": "The decision reason requires consideration of outcomes with less than 20% probability (here, only the 10% outcome in B) and a 10-point increase in their weight (to 20%). The individual does not mention this adjustment or any such rule. Instead, the individual evaluates the risk of losing more money (6000 vs. 3000 euros) and perceives the 55% chance of a large loss as too high. The individual does not refer to weighting or adjusting probabilities, nor do they compute a weighted sum with adjusted probabilities. Therefore, the individual did not apply the decision reason. The reasoning is based on intuitive risk perception, not on the formal rule of increasing small-probability weights. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
